 **Supersession** — HLD is versioned. Creating a new version is a human and business decision — the lifecycle never creates one automatically. When the team decides to cut a new version, the old version folder is kept as history and the README router is updated to point to the new active version. In-progress deviations always land in the current active version.
 
-**Archival** — `{{SKILL_PREFIX}}dev complete` archives a story after doc consistency review, evidence-backed terminal resolutions in the single Review Findings ledger, and passing required acceptance/checks. The archived folder keeps its original ASCII name (`[TICKET] name`); done status lives in the report, not the folder name. Routine LLD lag is a doc-update task; deviation auditing compares implementation to HLD only. Archived stories are read-only references.
+**Archival** — `{{SKILL_PREFIX}}dev complete` archives a story after doc consistency review, evidence-backed terminal resolutions in the single Review Findings ledger, and passing required acceptance/checks. The archived folder keeps its original ASCII name (`[TICKET] name`); done status lives in the report, not the folder name. Routine LLD lag is a doc-update task; deviation auditing compares implementation to HLD only. Archived stories are read-only references. One exception: an OG frontmatter migration (`docs/.og/cli.mjs migrate`, or a writer filling `description`/`tags` it reported) may edit the frontmatter of approved and archived Story files. It never changes their body.
+
+**Navigation** — `index.md` files are navigation, not docs. A bundle root's `index.md` carries only `okf_version: '0.2'`; every other `index.md` has no frontmatter. Writers keep their bullets current whenever they add, rename, move or remove a doc. Overview prose lives in `00 Overview.md`. The operational graph never indexes or writes an `index.md` or `log.md`, except the docs-site home `docs/index.md`.
 
